  "question": {
    "text": "Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math> be a relation on <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#8477;</mi></math>, given by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>{</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>:</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>a</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>b</mi><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mn>7</mn></msqrt></math> is an irrational number <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>}</mo></math>. Then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math> is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "X23ug",
      "text": "Reflexive but neither symmetric nor transitive",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "tUk3R",
      "text": "Reflexive and transitive but not symmetric",
      "isCorrect": false,
